NAME
       wall - send a message to every logged-in terminal

SYNOPSIS
       wall [MESSAGE]

DESCRIPTION
       wall (write to all) shows MESSAGE, or the text read from standard
       input, on the terminal of every user who is logged in, under a
       "Broadcast message from ..." heading. Administrators use it to warn
       users before a reboot. shutdown sends such a message by itself.

EXAMPLES
           wall 'server1 restarts in 10 minutes. Please save your work.'

SEE ALSO
       shutdown(8), who(1), write(1)
